<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="/markets">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/rfid">RFID</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">RFID Tire Tags</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">RFID products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/rfid/rfid-cards"><span class="abbr">RC</span><span class="label">RFID Smart Cards</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/rfid/rfid-tags-inlays"><span class="abbr">TI</span><span class="label">RFID Tags &amp; Inlays</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/rfid/rfid-tire-tags"><span class="abbr">TT</span><span class="label">RFID Tire Tags</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us your specifications and we&rsquo;ll take it from there.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">RFID &middot; RFID Tire Tags</div><h1 class="mk-h1">RFID tire tags</h1><p class="mk-lede">Hana manufactures rubber-embeddable UHF tire tags using inlay and strap constructions encapsulated in materials selected for integration into the tire and exposure to the curing process. The same automated RFID manufacturing capability also supports card, logistics and industrial-tag formats.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="#specialize-rfid-tire-tags" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><!-- data-yt accepts a YouTube video ID or a full URL; nothing loads from YouTube until play is pressed --><button type="button" class="wr-video yt-facade" data-yt="tS9fa12OV7I" aria-label="Play the Hana RFID tire tagging video on YouTube"><img src="/images/photos/oh-video-tire-tagging.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="wr-video-tag">YouTube</span><span class="wr-video-play" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="22" height="24" viewBox="0 0 16 18" fill="none"><path d="M0 0L16 9L0 18V0Z" fill="#0E4A7C"/></svg></span></button></div></div></section><section class="wr-sec" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--surface) 0%,var(--surface) 34%,var(--bg) 78%);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><img class="wr-bg" src="/images/photos/mk-rfid-tire-warehouse.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" /><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:60px;padding-bottom:60px;position:relative;z-index:1;"><div class="wr-grid"><div><h2 class="mk-h2">Why Hana RFID?</h2><p class="mk-body" style="margin:14px 0 26px;">Hana RFID is dedicated to the Tire Industry, designing and producing Tire Tags 24/7. With a network of local, State-of-the-Art production facilities and warehouses, Hana is able to support its customers locally on all major continents.</p><a class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" href="https://hanarfid.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Visit Hana RFID <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div><div class="wr-stats"><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="trophy"></i><div class="v">Global #1</div><div class="l">Embeddable Tire Tag Manufacturer</div></div><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="disc-3"></i><div class="v">Over 250 million</div><div class="l">Tires Tagged (2025)</div></div><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="history"></i><div class="v">Since 2005</div><div class="l">Global Tire Tag Design and Manufacturing</div></div><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="file-badge"></i><div class="v">Certified and Approved</div><div class="l">By all Major Tire Manufacturers</div></div><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="cpu"></i><div class="v">IC Independent</div><div class="l">Offering includes Impinj, NXP, ASYGN, Oxzon, etc.</div></div><div class="wr-stat"><i data-lucide="scan-line"></i><div class="v">100% Quality Tested</div><div class="l">Reading, writing and power</div></div></div><div class="wr-logos"><div class="wr-logos-lb">Certifications &amp; partners</div><div class="wr-logos-row"><div class="wr-logo"><img src="/images/partners/impinj-nxp.webp" alt="Impinj and NXP Gold Partner" loading="lazy"></div><div class="wr-logo"><img src="/images/partners/arc-quality.webp" alt="ARC Quality 2025, Auburn University RFID Lab" loading="lazy"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-rfid-tire-tags" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Tire tags are built on the same RFID process base as Hana's inlays, with materials, encapsulation and test selected for embedding in the tire.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Rubber-embeddable UHF tags</span></div><div class="desc">UHF inlay and strap constructions encapsulated in rubber-compatible materials for integration into the tire.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">High-speed automated production</span></div><div class="desc">Manufactured using Hana's automated roll-to-roll RFID processes.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Post-cure verification and unique ID</span></div><div class="desc">Read-performance verification after cure, with unique identification available for each tag.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">See RFID &amp; Smart Tags for the antenna, chip-attach, encapsulation and test processes behind these tags.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/rfid-smart-tags">Explore RFID &amp; Smart Tags <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build tags</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ohio"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">USA</span></span><div class="nm">Ohio</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How is a tire tag built to take being embedded in a tire?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">A tire tag is embedded in rubber during vulcanization, so it must withstand cure temperatures above 150°C and then repeated flex and temperature exposure throughout the tire's service life. The antenna, chip attach and encapsulation materials are selected for this environment, and read performance can be verified after cure.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How does tire-tag manufacturing relate to Hana's wider RFID capability?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Tire tags use the same core inlay, strap-attach and roll-to-roll manufacturing capability as Hana's wider RFID portfolio, with additional material and process requirements for embedding and cure.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Where does Hana build tire tags?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Tire tags are built in Lamphun, Thailand and Ohio, USA, with the site confirmed per program.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What frequency and protocol do the tags use?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">UHF across 860–960 MHz to ISO 18000-63 / EPC Gen 2. Other protocols can be considered to program requirements.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Can Hana support the antenna design as well as production?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Yes. Hana can work with the customer on antenna geometry and encapsulation material selection so the tag can be qualified against the required tire compound, geometry and production process before volume manufacturing.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What quality systems cover tire tags?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">ISO 9001 applies group-wide and IATF 16949 applies to automotive work. Every tag is encoded and read-verified, with per-unit traceability.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:32px;"><a href="/markets/rfid" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the RFID market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your tire-tag program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>

